nd Königsee in 2016. At the 2017 Worlds in Igls " [:a {:href "/athletes/109947"} "Tatjana Hüfner"] " won her fifth gold, and Geisenberger was only sixth after a weak first run, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/109957"} "Erin Hamlin"] " (USA) and " [:a {:href "/athletes/127510"} "Kim McRae"] " (CAN) in second and third. Three weeks before the Olympics " [:a {:href "/athletes/119457"} "Tatyana Ivanova"] " (RUS) won the European title in Sigulda, beating Geisenberger and " [:a {:href "/athletes/127944"} "Sandra Robatscher"] " (ITA)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In PyeongChang Geisenberger was in the lead after the first run and was never threatened. " [:a {:href "/athletes/137315"} "Dajana Eitberger"] " (GER) was the third-ranked German competitor but surprised many by winning the silver medal. " [:a {:href "/athletes/109962"} "Alex Gough"] " (CAN) had a great fourth run, and passed Hüfner for the bronze medal. Gough won Canada’s first ever medal in luge."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Run #1"] [:th {} "Run #2"] [:th {} "Run #3"] [:th {} "Run #4"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/119444"} "Natalie Geisenberger"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "3:05.232"] [:td {} "46.245 (1)"] [:td {} "46.209 (3)"] [:td {} "46.280 (1)"] [:td {} "46.498 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/137315"} "Dajana Eitberger"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GER.png"}] "GER"]] [:td {} "3:05.599"] [:td {} "46.381 (7)"] [:td {} "46.193 (2)"] [:td {} "46.57